\title{Require}
\date{2026-06-12T21:29:30Z}
\import{swarm-macros}

\p{There is a special \sf{require} directive which requires a specific device to be equipped.  Given the framework for requirements tracking, the typing rule is straightforward:

\rules{
    \swty{\Gamma}{\require{d}}{\Cmd{(\varnothing,\{d\},\varnothing)}{\Unit}}{\varnothing}
}

Note that #{d} must be a \em{literal} device name; otherwise we cannot \em{statically} infer the type of \require{d}.
}
